ui-there-are-two-color-configurations = There are two color configurations:

ui-standard-a-low-emphasis-color-scheme-best-used-for-focusing-attention-on-the-body-content = Standard: A low-emphasis color scheme best used for focusing attention on the body content.

ui-vibrant-a-high-emphasis-color-scheme-that-draws-attention-to-the-controls-it-can-also-indi = Vibrant: A high-emphasis color scheme that draws attention to the controls. It can also indicate a temporary change in the page behavior, such as entering edit mode.

ui-consider-using-alternative-color-roles-to-create-greater-or-lesser-emphasis-depending-on-t = Consider using alternative color roles to create greater or lesser emphasis depending on the needs of the app.

ui-toolbars-navigation-bars = Toolbars & navigation bars

ui-the-toolbar-and-navigation-bar-are-both-placed-at-the-bottom-of-the-window-so-should-not-b = The toolbar and navigation bar are both placed at the bottom of the window, so should not be shown at the same time. Show the navigation bar on primary pages, and toolbars on subsequent pages with actions.

ui-floating-toolbars-can-be-used-as-tabs-between-related-subsequent-pages-in-the-product-hier = Floating toolbars can be used as tabs between related subsequent pages in the product hierarchy. This helps group similar pages together, and shows that the selection affects the body content underneath.

ui-keep-navigation-distinct-and-use-a-toolbar-to-display-local-navigation-on-a-specific-page = Keep navigation distinct, and use a toolbar to display local navigation on a specific page

ui-consider-the-existing-app-hierarchy-when-using-a-toolbar-for-local-navigation-avoid-redund = Consider the existing app hierarchy when using a toolbar for local navigation. Avoid redundant or confusing navigation combinations in the same view.

ui-don-t-show-a-navigation-bar-and-a-toolbar-with-navigation-controls-at-the-same-time = Don't show a navigation bar and a toolbar with navigation controls at the same time

ui-the-docked-toolbar-s-container-spans-the-full-width-of-the-window-avoid-applying-rounded-c = The docked toolbar's container spans the full width of the window. Avoid applying rounded corners to the container. This can imply the container expands or changes upon interaction.

ui-as-long-as-there-s-a-minimum-of-16dp-padding-on-the-leading-and-trailing-edge-arrange-cont = As long as there's a minimum of 16dp padding on the leading and trailing edge, arrange controls inside however you see fit. The 32dp padding between items is just the default. All elements need a minimum 48x48dp target area to be accessible.

ui-be-cautious-of-including-too-many-controls-as-it-can-be-overwhelming = Be cautious of including too many controls as it can be overwhelming.

ui-don-t-overwhelm-people-with-too-many-controls = Don't overwhelm people with too many controls

ui-the-floating-toolbar-s-container-should-be-fully-visible-on-screen-if-more-actions-are-nee = The floating toolbar's container should be fully visible on screen. If more actions are needed, use an overflow menu.

ui-choose-the-most-essential-actions-to-show-on-screen-by-default = Choose the most essential actions to show on screen by default

ui-floating-toolbars-shouldn-t-exceed-the-edge-of-the-window-or-pane = Floating toolbars shouldn't exceed the edge of the window or pane

ui-floating-toolbars-have-elevation-by-default-if-the-content-beneath-the-toolbar-is-visually = Floating toolbars have elevation by default. If the content beneath the toolbar is visually distinct, elevation can be removed.

ui-the-elevation-on-floating-toolbars-can-be-removed-if-on-a-visually-distinct-background = The elevation on floating toolbars can be removed if on a visually distinct background

ui-when-configuring-a-toolbar-think-of-it-as-a-container-with-several-slots-these-slots-can-b = When configuring a toolbar, think of it as a container with several slots. These slots can be populated by buttons, icon buttons, images, text fields, or any kind of custom component. Icon buttons provide an even hierarchy of controls. Mixing in a filled icon button can help add emphasis to a single action.

ui-toolbars-are-made-of-slots-that-can-contain-many-kinds-of-actions = Toolbars are made of slots that can contain many kinds of actions

ui-visually-emphasizing-a-single-action-more-than-others-is-an-effective-way-to-create-hierar = Visually emphasizing a single action more than others is an effective way to create hierarchy and guide people to controls they use most often. Avoid emphasizing more than one action at a time. Some common ways to add emphasis to toolbar actions include:

ui-use-different-icon-button-color-styles-such-as-filled-tonal-and-standard = Use different icon button color styles, such as filled, tonal, and standard

ui-customize-the-color-roles-of-a-single-action-such-as-a-primary-or-secondary-palette = Customize the color roles of a single action, such as a primary or secondary palette

ui-use-wide-and-narrow-icon-buttons = Use wide and narrow icon buttons

ui-pair-the-toolbar-with-a-fab = Pair the toolbar with a FAB

ui-two-different-ways-to-create-a-high-emphasis-action-in-toolbars = Two different ways to create a high emphasis action in toolbars

ui-don-t-emphasize-multiple-buttons-with-bold-primary-colors-such-as-a-button-and-fab-togethe = Don't emphasize multiple buttons with bold, primary colors, such as a button and FAB together. Emphasize one action at a time.

ui-avoid-mixing-too-many-different-controls-in-the-same-toolbar-a-consistent-control-design-k = Avoid mixing too many different controls in the same toolbar. A consistent control design keeps things clear.

ui-avoid-using-square-icon-buttons-in-floating-toolbars-their-square-shape-conflicts-with-the = Avoid using square icon buttons in floating toolbars. Their square shape conflicts with the fully-rounded shape of the floating toolbar container. Square buttons can be used in the docked toolbar.

ui-don-t-use-square-filled-icon-buttons-in-floating-toolbars = Don't use square filled icon buttons in floating toolbars

ui-a-fab-can-be-placed-next-to-a-floating-toolbar-to-present-one-high-priority-action-alongsi = A FAB can be placed next to a floating toolbar to present one high-priority action alongside a unified set of toolbar actions. Use a FAB for the highest-priority action in the view, or to complement the controls.

ui-floating-toolbars-can-be-paired-with-fabs = Floating toolbars can be paired with FABs

ui-only-place-docked-toolbars-at-the-bottom-of-the-window-if-using-other-bottom-aligned-eleme = Only place docked toolbars at the bottom of the window. If using other bottom-aligned elements, such as a navigation bar, don't use a docked toolbar.

ui-docked-toolbars-are-always-at-the-bottom-of-the-window = Docked toolbars are always at the bottom of the window

ui-floating-toolbars-can-be-horizontal-or-vertical-horizontal-toolbars-should-have-a-minimum = Floating toolbars can be horizontal or vertical. Horizontal toolbars should have a minimum 16dp margin from the edge of the window.

ui-horizontal-floating-toolbars-should-be-at-least-16dp-from-the-edge-of-the-window = Horizontal floating toolbars should be at least 16dp from the edge of the window

ui-in-larger-breakpoints-floating-toolbars-can-be-vertical-and-placed-on-either-side-of-the-s = In larger breakpoints, floating toolbars can be vertical and placed on either side of the screen. Vertical toolbars should have a minimum 24dp margin.

ui-maintain-at-least-a-24dp-margin-for-vertical-toolbars = Maintain at least a 24dp margin for vertical toolbars

ui-to-keep-vertical-toolbars-compact-don-t-use-wide-icon-buttons-use-narrow-or-default-icon-b = To keep vertical toolbars compact, don't use wide icon buttons. Use narrow or default icon buttons instead.

ui-using-wide-buttons-with-vertical-toolbars-can-unnecessarily-widen-toolbar-containers-and-h = Using wide buttons with vertical toolbars can unnecessarily widen toolbar containers and hide other UI elements

ui-vertical-toolbars-should-be-positioned-opposite-the-navigation-rail-to-balance-out-the-scr = Vertical toolbars should be positioned opposite the navigation rail to balance out the screen and keep actions easy to access. When showing a navigation rail and vertical floating toolbar at once, use the centered configuration of the navigation rail.

ui-when-a-nav-rail-is-visible-the-floating-toolbar-should-be-vertical-on-the-opposite-edge-of = When a nav rail is visible, the floating toolbar should be vertical on the opposite edge of the window

ui-docked-the-docked-toolbar-should-always-span-100-of-the-screen-width-in-compact-breakpoint = Docked: The docked toolbar should always span 100% of the screen width. In compact breakpoints, elements in the toolbar should be evenly spaced. In medium breakpoints and larger, adjust the padding between controls to create a comfortable layout by centering all elements, or by centering a key action and aligning other elements to the edges.

ui-docked-toolbar-items-should-be-evenly-spaced-in-compact-windows = Docked toolbar items should be evenly spaced in compact windows

ui-in-medium-breakpoints-and-larger-create-a-spacious-layout-by-centering-all-elements = In medium breakpoints and larger, create a spacious layout by centering all elements

ui-align-controls-to-the-edge-of-the-screen-to-make-them-easier-to-reach-on-tablets-and-to-be = Align controls to the edge of the screen to make them easier to reach on tablets, and to better highlight a primary action in the middle

ui-on-web-and-large-screens-the-docked-toolbar-can-be-rounded-dividers-can-be-used-to-organiz = On web and large screens, the docked toolbar can be rounded. Dividers can be used to organize large amounts of items. Only shrink the height and use extra small buttons if vertical space is limited.

ui-on-web-and-other-large-screens-docked-toolbars-can-be-rounded-and-placed-in-different-part = On web and other large screens, docked toolbars can be rounded and placed in different parts of the page

ui-floating-the-container-should-only-be-as-big-as-needed-to-hold-the-items-inside-before-rea = Floating: The container should only be as big as needed to hold the items inside before reaching the 16dp margin. If there's not enough space for all items, put them in an overflow menu in the trailing slot. As the breakpoint expands, more actions can be revealed. The floating toolbar width can also be capped to keep it smaller and hide more elements.

ui-don-t-add-extra-space-to-a-toolbar-beyond-its-necessary-items = Don't add extra space to a toolbar beyond its necessary items

ui-at-larger-screen-sizes-the-container-can-display-more-controls-before-hitting-the-16dp-mar = At larger screen sizes, the container can display more controls before hitting the 16dp margin

ui-vertical-toolbars-aren-t-recommended-for-compact-windows-they-take-up-a-significant-area-o = Vertical toolbars aren't recommended for compact windows. They take up a significant area of the screen and may feel visually overwhelming, especially on screens with complex layouts. Only use them when the screen is simple or when the toolbar has a few controls.

ui-vertical-toolbars-can-cover-important-content-in-compact-windows = Vertical toolbars can cover important content in compact windows

ui-in-larger-breakpoints-floating-toolbars-can-be-aligned-to-opposite-edges-of-the-screen-so = In larger breakpoints, floating toolbars can be aligned to opposite edges of the screen so they're easy to reach and group similar actions. For example, consider placing the undo and redo actions in one toolbar, and editing controls in another. Stylistic differences can help emphasize each toolbar's purpose and clarify hierarchy.

ui-multiple-toolbars-with-different-stylistic-treatments-can-create-hierarchy-and-distinguish = Multiple toolbars with different stylistic treatments can create hierarchy and distinguish different kinds of actions

ui-don-t-use-multiple-toolbars-in-compact-windows-there-typically-isn-t-enough-room-on-screen = Don't use multiple toolbars in compact windows. There typically isn't enough room on screen. Instead, use one toolbar for all actions.

ui-avoid-using-multiple-toolbars-in-smaller-windows = Avoid using multiple toolbars in smaller windows

ui-actions-at-the-trailing-edge-of-the-toolbar-can-collapse-into-an-overflow-menu-at-smaller = Actions at the trailing edge of the toolbar can collapse into an overflow menu at smaller breakpoints, and become visible again at larger sizes. Use the window size control above to compare both states.

ui-in-right-to-left-rtl-languages-mirror-individual-items-that-need-it-like-icons-and-text-di = In right-to-left (RTL) languages, mirror individual items that need it, like icons and text direction. If the order of actions is important, flip the order of the actions as well.

ui-docked-toolbars-can-either-remain-on-the-screen-during-scroll-or-animate-offscreen-floatin = Docked toolbars can either remain on the screen during scroll, or animate offscreen. Floating toolbars can remain on the screen, animate offscreen, or collapse into a single, high-emphasis action on scroll.

ui-use-the-controls-below-to-move-the-toolbar-offscreen-or-collapse-it-to-its-key-action-only = Use the controls below to move the toolbar offscreen or collapse it to its key action. Only one transition is available at a time.

